<title>BELGIUM: Full effect of Italy's eurotax allowed.</title>
<headline>Full effect of Italy's eurotax allowed.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission confirmed on Friday that Italy's proposed eurotax would now be allowed in full for 1997 budget.</p>
<p>Eurostat, the EU's statistical arm, ruled on Friday that a portion of the tax, representing 0.2 percent of GDP, would now be allowed. But Commission officials stressed that the remaining portion of the tax -- 0.4 percent of GDP -- was not under dispute in this latest review.</p>
<p>Therefore the entire tax, representing 0.6 percent of GDP, can now be applied towards the 1997 budget deficit. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
